three of the five indirect-question clauses in that are clear cases of abnormal order—how is it instead of how it is, to whom does it owe instead of to whom it owes, & by whom is it paid instead of by whom it is paid—;
===
three of the five indirect-question clauses in that are clear cases of abnormal order—*how is it* instead of *how it is,* *to whom does it owe* instead of *to whom it owes,* & *by whom is it paid* instead of *by whom it is paid*—;
